{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chuanle song\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -Raw 'pipeline/references/autonomous_design.md'; Get-Content -Raw 'pipeline/decisions/20260926-183336_route_change.md'; Get-Content -Raw 'pipeline/designs/exp_design_20260926-183100.md'; Get-Content -Raw 'pipeline/reviews/motivation_review_20260926-183100.md'\"","aggregated_output":"Get-Content: \r\nLine |\r\n   2 |  Get-Content -Raw 'pipeline/references/autonomous_design.md'; Get-Cont …\r\n     |  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\r\n     | 找不到路径“D:\\project\\AdaRES_project\\pipeline\\references\\autonomous_design.md”，因为该路径不存在。\r\n# AdaRES_project 决策记录\n\n- **时间**: 2026-09-26 18:33:36\n- **类型**: route_change\n- **问题**: G1 best 0.4980 and three distinct confidence diagnoses N1/N2/N3: admit either of two available GPU slots?\n- **决策**: Close G1; reject N1 detach-only, N2 inference grouping and N3 collision-only routes; leave server-2 GPUs 0/1 unqueued\n- **依据**: G1 -0.0114 vs B4-E30; N1 mixed gradients and negligible controlled one-step separation; N2 language nearest same-object 121/441; N3 collisions 6/365 native pairs; six admission gates not satisfied\n- **证据**: pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-G1_done_complete_20260926-183100.md; pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-N1-N3_diagnosis_20260926-183100.md; pipeline/research_work.json\n\r\n# Experiment Design - AdaRES_project\n\n2026-09-26 18:31 Asia/Shanghai\n\n## 1. Motivation\nGoal: \"AdaRES: improve a faithful standard-indicator 3D referring expression segmentation baseline by learning query confidence from metric-aligned evidence, targeting ScanRefer mIoU >= 0.515.\" Capacity gap 2/2 with candidate budget 2. This cycle attempted distinct N1/N2/N3 confidence mechanisms after G1 terminal reconciliation.\n\n## 2. Current Best Results\n| ID | State | mIoU | Acc@0.25 | Acc@0.5 | spmIoU |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| B1 | complete | 0.5020 | 0.610 | 0.553 | 0.467 |\n| B4-E30 | champion | 0.5094 | 0.608 | 0.562 | 0.474 |\n| H5 | early stop | 0.5061 | unavailable | unavailable | unavailable |\n| G1 | complete | 0.4980 | unavailable | unavailable | unavailable |\n\n## 3. Analysis & Direction\nG1's terminal metric and paired 16-scene mask/selection audit disconfirm its metric-target route. N1 gradient opposition is inconsistent and its detach-only intervention is an ablation. N2 same-object selection inconsistency is real under oracle grouping, but language-nearest and mask-overlap proxies are unreliable. N3 qualifying distinct-target collisions occur in just 6/365 native pairs over 64 scenes.\n\n## 4. Experiment Plan\nNo candidate admitted. N1 fails an independent mechanism and repeatable functional diagnosis; N2 fails inference-valid grouping/control; N3 fails task-relevant incidence for its collision-only loss. Candidate budget is a maximum, not a quota. No model/config, receipt, sync, or dispatch is authorized. A future distinct route must predeclare mechanism, paired native control, backward reachability, resources, independence and all goal constraints.\n\n## 5. GPU Allocation Plan\nServer-2 GPU0 and GPU1 remain unassigned by this project's queue. Both were used transiently for read-only diagnostics, now complete. Server-6 excluded. No live GPU utilization is inferred from an empty project queue.\n\n## 6. Implementation Checklist\n- [x] Reconcile G1 terminal status and compare with champion.\n- [x] Run N1 native gradient/control, N2 oracle-group and inference-proxy, N3 native training-pair incidence diagnostics.\n- [x] Preserve raw evidence and route decisions.\n- [ ] No model package/config, training receipt, commit/sync or queue entry until a new candidate passes all six admission hard gates.\n\n## 7. Risk Assessment\nSmall fixed cohorts are observational. G1/B4 checkpoints differ in trained state, not a freshly matched randomized control. N1's one-parameter SGD probe does not represent full training. N2 uses validation labels only for analysis, never deployable inference. N3's 64 scenes are a bounded incidence screen.\n\n## 8. Smell Check\nDetaching existing evidence alone is pure ablation; adjusting a collision weight or language similarity threshold on validation would be tuning. None is admitted as a renamed candidate.\n\nStatus: NO ADMISSION. Independent tested routes N1, N2 and N3 do not pass diagnosis/controls. This does not assert global scientific exhaustion; resume on a new, independently justified mechanism with a native executable test.\n\r\n# Motivation Review - AdaRES_project\n\n2026-09-26 18:31 Asia/Shanghai\n\n## 1. Goal\nGoal: \"AdaRES: improve a faithful standard-indicator 3D referring expression segmentation baseline by learning query confidence from metric-aligned evidence, targeting ScanRefer mIoU >= 0.515.\" Baseline B1 0.5020, champion B4-E30 0.5094, target gap 0.0056. Constraints: server-2 GPUs 0/1 only, one independent experiment per GPU, B2/B4 continuation protocol fixed, released SPFormer backbone and project decoder, report mIoU/Acc@0.25/Acc@0.5/active queries/latency/peak memory, no validation tuning of thresholds, temperatures, weights, feature sets or epochs. Bans: no server-6, no released b005/CFNet as B0, no ranking-margin or occupancy-loss-weight scan.\n\n## 2. Story Status\n| Hypothesis | Status | Evidence | Gap |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Competition-aware query confidence | Partial | B4-E30 0.5094 | Below target; no fresh matched control |\n| Metric-IoU target | Negative | G1 0.4980; paired mask and selection quality decline | No G1 successor without independent evidence |\n| Gradient interference | Mixed | N1 cosines -0.868 to +0.194 in trained batches | No repeatable functional benefit from detach-only |\n| Cross-expression agreement | Proxy failure | N2 oracle-group inconsistency, language nearest same-object 27.4% | Inference-valid grouping |\n| Distinct-target collisions | Sparse | N3 6/365 native pairs | Insufficient occurrence for collision-only loss |\n\n## 3. Experiment Assessment\nB1 0.5020, B4-E30 0.5094; B2-E30 0.5058, D1 0.5080, F4 0.5060, H5 0.5061 and G1 0.4980 do not reach the target. G1 fell 0.0114 below B4-E30. Previous E/H/J/K/L/M diagnoses closed their specific routes; the new N1/N2/N3 screens do not reopen them.\n\n## 4. Gap Analysis\nThe first 16 validation scenes expose substantial oracle-versus-selected headroom, but oracle selection is unavailable at inference. No reproducible, label-free new confidence signal with matched native control and all six hard gates was established this tick. Active queries, full-run latency/peak memory and evaluation noise remain unquantified.\n\n## 5. Design Rationale\nN1 tested whether confidence gradients impede mask learning; N2 tested whether a second expression could identify a referent consistently; N3 tested whether distinct-target co-occurrence gave a native exclusivity signal. Each addresses a different causal path. Their bounded tests failed to yield an admissible mechanism; a loss weight, similarity threshold, detach-only ablation or renamed fusion would not repair the missing evidence.\n\n## 6. Next Batch\nNo training admission. See `pipeline/designs/exp_design_20260926-183100.md`. Resume at the next research window with independent prospective evidence and a concrete native diagnosis/control, while maintaining the six admission gates.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
